.TH tuhexedit n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuhexedit
.PP
Small binary read/write/search/patch helpers in pure Tcl.
.PP
\fBtuhexedit\fR is a library module, not a GUI editor. It builds on \fBtclutils::tubin\fR and reuses \fBtclutils::tuhexdump\fR for dump output.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tuhexedit 0.1
.CE
.SS "Read bytes"
.CS
set bytes [::tclutils::tuhexedit::readBytes file.bin 0x100 32]
.CE
.SS "Write bytes"
.CS
::tclutils::tuhexedit::writeBytes file.bin 0x100 $bytes
.CE
.PP
By default this creates \fBfile.bin.bak\fR. Pass \fB0\fR as fourth argument to disable backup creation:
.CS
::tclutils::tuhexedit::writeBytes file.bin 0x100 $bytes 0
.CE
.SS Search
.CS
::tclutils::tuhexedit::findHex file.bin {50 4B 03 04}
::tclutils::tuhexedit::findString file.bin content.xml
.CE
.PP
Both commands return a list of byte offsets.
.SS Patch
.CS
::tclutils::tuhexedit::patch file.bin 0x100 {50 4B 03 04}
::tclutils::tuhexedit::patch file.bin 0x100 {50 4B} -backup 0
.CE
.SS Dump
.CS
puts [::tclutils::tuhexedit::dump file.bin -offset 0 -length 128]
.CE
.PP
The dump command delegates to \fBtclutils::tuhexdump\fR.
.SS Limits
.PP
\fBpatch\fR and \fBwriteBytes\fR are in\-place, length\-preserving operations. They do not insert or delete bytes and therefore do not shift the remaining file content.
.PP
\fBfindHex\fR, \fBfindString\fR, and \fBpatch\fR currently read the complete file into memory. \fBreadBytes\fR is the partial\-read API for large files.
